Verify is instructions, not a tool name. Inspect the runtime entrypoint, responsible source and regression assertion. Reconcile source evidence with the frozen target and authored current/sketch; missing evidence stays unknown. The assertion must distinguish reported failure from target. Suite exit0 and worker reports prove neither coverage nor correctness; already-correct work needs observed evidence without mandatory edits.
Run Verify actions independently, then the paired check episode (acceptance FIRST, configured suite LAST); later Bash or edits require a fresh whole episode. Do not modify artifacts, checks or gates. Never claim a command ran without its settled result.
Use one tool call per reply and wait. Begin the final answer with PASS for observed acceptance, FAIL for an observed unmet condition, or UNVERIFIED with a concrete reason; include required Behavior after the verdict on the same line.
